* opamp_core open-loop AC testbench, `klt sim` circuit BODY (issue #77)
*
* Fleet-executable twin of opamp_ac.spice.tmpl: same DC-servo open-loop
* technique (Rfb out->inn, Cfb inn->gnd) and the same measurement definitions
* (DC gain at 1 Hz, unity-gain frequency, phase at unity gain, Iq/Pq at the
* operating point). klt supplies the .lib/.temp/alter-vdd cards and the
* .control block; the analysis and the `.meas` cards live in the request
* (bin/pvt_sweep.py build_klt_request). The same body serves two requests:
* `ac` (the sweep and gain/GBW/phase measurements) and `ac-iq` (a zero-offset
* `dc` point of Vinp = the AC bias point, measuring Iq -- the fleet runner takes
* `.meas` cards only, and `.meas` has no operating-point type).
* The DUT is wrapped in a subckt so a candidate netlist selected with
* --netlist is included unmodified (ports: vdd vss inn inp out ibias).
* The common-mode level follows each corner's own VDD (`alter vdd`): VDD/2.

.option scale=1u

.subckt opamp_dut vdd vss inn inp out ibias
.include "{OPAMP_NETLIST}"
.ends opamp_dut

Vdd vdd 0 dc {VDD_NOM}
Vss vss 0 dc 0
Iref vdd ibias dc {IBIAS_A}
Bcm cm 0 V = 0.5*v(vdd)
Vinp inp cm dc 0 ac 1
Xdut vdd vss inn inp out ibias opamp_dut
Rfb out inn {RFB}
Cfb inn 0 {CFB}
Cload out 0 {CL_F}
